{{also|Hunky}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhʌŋ.ki/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-hunky.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌŋki|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{suf|en|hunk|y|id2=adjectival}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} Exhibiting strong, masculine beauty.
# Shaped like a [[hunk]], or piece; [[chunky]].
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} All right; in good condition.
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} [[even]]; [[square]]; on equal footing ''with''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1900|author={{w|Stephen Crane}}|title=Wounds in the Rain|passage={{...}} he dropped like a brick into the firing line and began to shoot; began to get "'''hunky'''" with all those people who had been plugging at him.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der2|en|hunky punk|hunky-dory}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|hunk}}

===Etymology 2===
From the older {{m|en||*hunk}}, probably alteration of {{m|en|Hungarian}} {{suf|en||-y|alt2=-ie/-y|id2=diminutive}}. Compare {{m|en|bohunk}} and {{m|en|honky}} / {{m|en|honkey}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|hunkie|hunkey}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|slang|now|uncommon|ethnic slur}} A [[Hungarian]] or other eastern European, e.g. a [[Romanian]] or a [[Slav]]. {{q|Sometimes applied (like {{m|en|honky}}) to any [[white]] person.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1924|author=Jack Bethea|title=Bed Rock|page=175
|passage="All '''hunkies''' and wops, and no wonder there was seven hundred and fifty of them."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1940|title=Unemployment Compensation Interpretation Service: Benefit series|page=183
|passage=He made hunkies and cut ice-cream sandwiches.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1952|author=Chester Himes|title=Cast the First Stone|page=66
|passage=The night before I had let a '''hunky''' called Big John have a dollar's worth of chips in the poker game {{...}}}}
#* '''1969''', Robert Beck (Iceberg Slim), ''Trick Baby'', page 149:
#*: He said, "I'm going to buy this building and turn this into a Nigger bar. I'm going to bar all you fucking '''hunkies'''."
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=Josephine Wtulich|title=American Xenophobia and the Slav Immigrant: A Living Legacy of Mind and Spirit
|passage=On the negative side, a '''hunky''' was culturally schizophrenic, an inhabitant of crowded and ill-kept rooms and whose clothing was in poor taste, an alcoholic, intrinsically dull and stupid, an offspring of domineering parents, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Victor Bockris|title=Warhol: The Biography|page=20|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=NRmjRcSYXlgC&lpg=PA20&dq=hunkies&hl=ru&pg=PA20#v=onepage&q=hunkies&f=false|passage=Like blacks, who were the only ethnic group below them on the social scale, Eastern Europeans, contemptuously labelled ‘'''hunkies'''’, were dismissed as incapable and untrustworthy.}}

